WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.254
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.254 --> 00:00:15.600
Today, mods: what a mod is, what it can change in your world, and how to keep one from wrecking it.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.177
Click Mods up top.

6
00:00:18.177 --> 00:00:22.362
A mod is built just like a world, same editor and same sections,

7
00:00:22.362 --> 00:00:24.716
but it only holds the parts it adds.

8
00:00:24.716 --> 00:00:27.855
You just set its type to mod when you create it.

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.430
My mods lists the ones I've made and published: the Time Keeper,

10
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:37.658
Status Effects, Roll Card, and Mechs and Rides, each with its own ID and version.

11
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.765
Browse mods opens Discover, so you can find other people's.

12
00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:46.239
Ones you add go in active mods, in a numbered order you can move around.

13
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.232
Nothing changes until you press Apply.

14
00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:55.963
And applying writes the mod into your world for good: take the mod off later and what it added stays.

15
00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:57.829
So try mods on a copy first.

16
00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:01.491
Before you add a mod, review it.

17
00:01:01.491 --> 00:01:08.052
Every mod in the list has a Review draft contents button, so here's mine for the Time Keeper.

18
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.258
It's checked against the Workshop: nineteen entries across thirteen sections.

19
00:01:13.258 --> 00:01:18.264
Six are new, eleven would change things I already have, and two would be removed.

20
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.652
Changes yours marks every entry that would overwrite one of your own.

21
00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:29.393
A mod can change or remove what your world already has, so read this every time.

22
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:31.814
And here are its triggers, all new.

23
00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:37.020
Every one of them starts with TK, for Time Keeper, so none of them can land on top of yours.

24
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:41.006
That's the big rule if you make mods.

25
00:01:41.006 --> 00:01:46.639
When a mod and a world share an entry, saving can be refused over missing fields.

26
00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:50.533
So name your entries so no world will already have them.

27
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:54.775
Our example mod does it: every entry starts with Gilt Circus.

28
00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:57.264
And mods add up.

29
00:01:57.264 --> 00:02:01.997
Your world plus every mod has to fit inside the size limits together.

30
00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:05.357
Go over, and all you get is Failed to build mods,

31
00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:09.541
so take them off one at a time to find the one that broke it.

32
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:15.308
That's mods. Our example mod is linked in the description.

33
00:02:15.308 --> 00:02:21.568
Next time, publishing: the card, drafts, and keeping players happy through updates.

34
00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:25.981
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

